## Why This Is Asked
Testing idempotency and reliable streaming under global scale is critical for high-stakes financial and logistics systems where duplicate orders or missed events can cause significant business impact.

## Key Concepts
- Idempotency keys with Redis storage for duplicate prevention
- Exactly-once streaming using sequence IDs and consumer idempotence
- Cross-region consistency with multi-DC PostgreSQL and Kafka replication
- Fault injection testing for partial outages and latency budgets
- Contract testing for API and streaming interfaces

## Code Example
```javascript
async function testIdempotentCreate(client, orderPayload, idempotencyKey) {
  const res1 = await client.post('/orders', orderPayload, { 
    headers: { 'Idempotency-Key': idempotencyKey } 
  });
  const res2 = await client.post('/orders', orderPayload, { 
    headers: { 'Idempotency-Key': idempotencyKey } 
  });
  assert.equal(res1.status, 201);
  assert.equal(res2.status, 200);
  assert.equal(res1.body.id, res2.body.id);
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests reliability of composite APIs with dependent services.

## Key Concepts
- Downstream latency, timeouts, partial failures, circuit breakers
- Idempotent retries, exponential backoff, observability
- End-to-end timing and schema validation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo test using jest + nock
const nock = require('nock');
const request = require('supertest');
const app = require('../app');
test('partial data when one downstream times out', async () => {
  nock('http://sales').get('/daily').delay(3000).reply(200, {sales: 1000});
  nock('http://customers').get('/daily').reply(200, {customers: 50});
  const res = await request(app).get('/reports/daily');
  expect(res.statusCode).toBe(200);
  expect(res.body).toHaveProperty('sales');
  expect(res.headers).toHaveProperty('x-downstream-warn');
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test circuit-breaker behavior under sustained latency?
- What metrics would you validate in your observability stack?

